[
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name ∈ {\"check_user_risk_level\", \"get_stock_info\", \"search_market_news\", \"flag_compliance_issue\"} THEN ALLOW (read‑only tools are always permitted)."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = \"recommend_portfolio\" AND (check_user_risk_level_status IS MISSING OR check_user_risk_level_level IS MISSING) THEN DENY (a prior risk‑level check must exist)."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = \"recommend_portfolio\" AND lower(check_user_risk_level_status) ≠ \"success\" THEN DENY (the prior risk‑level check must have succeeded)."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = \"recommend_portfolio\" AND risk_level IS MISSING THEN DENY (the required risk_level argument is absent)."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = \"recommend_portfolio\" AND risk_level ≠ check_user_risk_level_level THEN DENY (the supplied risk_level must exactly match the verified user level)."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = \"recommend_portfolio\" AND NOT _risk_not_exceed(check_user_risk_level_level, risk_level) THEN DENY (the requested C‑level may not exceed the user's verified level)."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = \"recommend_portfolio\" AND recommend_portfolio_called = true AND check_user_risk_level_timestamp = recommend_portfolio_last_check_timestamp THEN DENY (a fresh risk check is required before a second recommend_portfolio call in the same episode)."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = \"recommend_portfolio\" AND recommend_portfolio_called = true AND (check_user_risk_level_timestamp IS MISSING OR recommend_portfolio_last_check_timestamp IS MISSING) THEN DENY (cannot verify freshness of risk check, so deny)."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = \"recommend_portfolio\" AND (get_stock_info_is_st = true OR get_stock_info_risk_rating = \"R5\") AND check_user_risk_level_level ≠ \"C5\" THEN DENY (ST stocks or R5 products may only be recommended to C5 users)."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = \"recommend_portfolio\" AND (get_stock_info_is_st = true OR get_stock_info_risk_rating = \"R5\") AND check_user_risk_level_level = \"C5\" THEN ALLOW (provided all other checks pass)."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = \"recommend_portfolio\" AND ANY product risk rating in the generated portfolio > USER_MAX_PRODUCT_RISK[check_user_risk_level_level] THEN DENY (portfolio must stay within the product‑risk band allowed for the user's level)."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF user makes any claim of urgency, hardship, authority, approval, or pastes documents AND tool_name = \"recommend_portfolio\" AND (check_user_risk_level_status IS MISSING OR lower(check_user_risk_level_status) ≠ \"success\") THEN DENY (user statements do not replace the required risk‑level verification)."
  }
]

**Rationale:**  
These IF‑THEN clauses capture every precondition the policy enforces before allowing the high‑risk `recommend_portfolio` tool and explicitly permit the safe, read‑only tools. They encode the need for a successful prior risk check, exact matching of the supplied risk level, prohibition of level escalation, one‑call‑per‑check enforcement, strict handling of ST/R5 stocks (only C5 users), and the requirement that the portfolio’s constituent products stay within the user’s allowable risk band. They also state that user‑generated assertions cannot substitute for the mandatory verification step. Together they provide a complete, checkable logical specification of the security request.

