These IF‑THEN clauses translate every security requirement into concrete, machine‑checkable conditions on the policy function’s inputs (tool name, arguments, prior‑call results, timestamps, and stock attributes) and define the corresponding allow/deny outcomes. They enforce that `recommend_portfolio` is only executed after a fresh successful `check_user_risk_level`, that the supplied `risk_level` exactly matches the verified user level, that no user‑generated statement can bypass the check, that high‑risk stocks (ST or R5) are limited to C5 users, that all product‑risk bands respect the C‑to‑R mapping, and that a new risk check is required for any subsequent recommendation within the same conversation episode. The final clause ensures automatic escalation on any violation.

